  "dialogue_steps": [
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "As time passed, I began a mural in Maia's garden. It held the places we'd known and the places we'd meant to find.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "I worked a little at a time. The wall was larger than any page I had used. Some days that helped.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "The tree needs to be wider here. We never left enough room for the creature to land.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "Then make it wider. It's your wall.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "Cassia helped me remember. We could disagree about a color, then fall quiet because we'd both thought of asking him.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "mural_remembrance",
      "text": "The garden gave the painting a life around it: water, leaves, people passing. I could go there when I wanted to be close to a memory.",
      "bg": "memory_mural"
    },
    {
      "scene": "treehouse_remembrance",
      "text": "We brought new drawings to the treehouse, and messages to Joren. There were still maps we hadn't finished. We made room for both.",
      "bg": "treehouse_memory"
    }
  ],
